  "problem": "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,0),(2,0),(2,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under a **clockwise** rotation of $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ radians about the origin?\n\nI. $(2,-2)$\n\nII. $(-1,-\\sqrt{3})$\n\nIII. $(\\sqrt{3},0)$",
